---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import ReadingOrder from '../../components/ReadingOrder';
import { supabaseClient } from '../../lib/supabaseClient';

const bookData = [
  {
    title: 'The Name of the Wind',
    slug: 'the-name-of-the-wind',
    status: 'mandatory' as const,
    note: 'Day one of Kvothe telling his story. Lyrical, slow-burn, unforgettable prose.',
    page_count: 662,
    publication_year: 2007,
  },
  {
    title: "The Wise Man's Fear",
    slug: 'the-wise-mans-fear',
    status: 'mandatory' as const,
    note: 'Day two. Longer, more divisive, but essential. The Adem sequences are polarising.',
    page_count: 994,
    publication_year: 2011,
  },
  {
    title: 'The Slow Regard of Silent Things',
    slug: 'the-slow-regard-of-silent-things',
    status: 'supplementary' as const,
    note: 'Novella about Auri alone in the Underthing. No plot — pure atmosphere. Read only if you loved Auri.',
    page_count: 159,
    publication_year: 2014,
  },
];

const bookSlugs = bookData.map(b => b.slug);
const { data: dbRows } = await supabaseClient.from('books').select('slug, cover_url, darkness_level, avg_rating, series, series_number').in('slug', bookSlugs);
const dbMap = new Map<string, any>((dbRows ?? []).map((r: any) => [r.slug, r]));
const books = bookData.map(b => { const db = dbMap.get(b.slug); return { ...b, cover_url: db?.cover_url ?? null, darkness_level: db?.darkness_level ?? null, avg_rating: db?.avg_rating ?? null, series_label: db?.series && db?.series_number != null ? `${db.series} #${db.series_number}` : null }; });

const totalPages = books.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (b.page_count ?? 0), 0);
const totalHours = Math.round(totalPages / 30);
---

<Layout
  title="The Kingkiller Chronicle Reading Order | Fantasy Obscura"
  description="Complete reading order for The Kingkiller Chronicle by Patrick Rothfuss."
>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <a href="/reading-orders" class="text-sm text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-800 transition-colors">← Reading Orders</a>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-purple-600 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Reading Order</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">The Kingkiller Chronicle</h1>
        <p class="mt-1 text-lg text-zinc-500">by Patrick Rothfuss</p>
      </div>
      <span class="mt-1 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-red-50 border border-red-200 text-red-700 text-sm font-medium">
        ⚠️ Incomplete — Book 3 unreleased
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 border-y border-zinc-100 py-4">
      <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="text-zinc-400">📚</span> 2 main novels + 1 novella</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="text-zinc-400">📄</span> ~{totalPages.toLocaleString()} pages</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="text-zinc-400">⏱</span> ~{totalHours} hours reading time</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="text-zinc-400">🕯️🕯️🕯️</span> Moderate darkness</span>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-5 text-base text-zinc-700 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      A legendary hero sits in a country inn and tells a scribe his life story over three days. Rothfuss writes with more craft and precision than almost anyone in the genre — and book 3 has been in development since 2011 with no release date.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Warning */}
  <div class="mb-8 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5">
    <p class="font-semibold text-amber-900 mb-2">⚠️ The series is unfinished</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-800">
      <em>The Doors of Stone</em> (book 3) has been announced since 2011 with no publication date as of 2026. Many readers prefer to wait before starting. The two published books end on open threads that may never resolve.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1">Reading Order</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mb-6">Start with The Name of the Wind. No other order is possible.</p>
    <ReadingOrder books={books} client:load />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 rounded-xl border bg-zinc-50 p-6">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">The Slow Regard of Silent Things</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-zinc-700 leading-relaxed">
      Rothfuss himself warns in the foreword that this novella is "not for everyone." It follows Auri — a side character from the main books — over seven days in the Underthing. There is almost no plot. It is a meditation. Only read it if you found Auri fascinating; otherwise skip it entirely without loss.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 rounded-xl border bg-zinc-50 p-6">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">What to expect</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-700">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400">→</span> Lyrical, carefully crafted prose — the most technically accomplished writing in mainstream fantasy.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400">→</span> Frame narrative — Kvothe is recounting his life, so there is dramatic irony built in from page one.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400">→</span> Magic system based on "sympathy" (physics-based) and "naming" (true language) — rigorously defined.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400">→</span> Slow-burn pacing. Book 1 covers Kvothe's first year at the University. Book 2, his second. This is intentional.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-zinc-400">→</span> Kvothe is an unreliable narrator — he is telling his own legend and may be embellishing.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 rounded-xl border bg-zinc-50 p-6">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-4">Darkness progression</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-1 sm:gap-4">
        <span class="font-medium text-zinc-700 sm:w-44 shrink-0">The Name of the Wind</span>
        <span class="text-zinc-400">🕯️🕯️🕯️</span>
        <span class="text-zinc-500">Poverty, loss, abuse — but youthful energy dominates</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-1 sm:gap-4">
        <span class="font-medium text-zinc-700 sm:w-44 shrink-0">The Wise Man's Fear</span>
        <span class="text-zinc-400">🕯️🕯️🕯️</span>
        <span class="text-zinc-500">War, assassins, fae — darker and more complex</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-zinc-400">Scale: 🕯️ Lighthearted → 🕯️🕯️🕯️🕯️🕯️ Brutal</p>
  </div>

  <div class="border-t pt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 justify-between">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-zinc-700 mb-2">Want more literary fantasy?</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/categories/epic" class="text-sm text-purple-600 hover:text-purple-800 underline underline-offset-2">Browse Epic Fantasy →</a>
        <a href="/craft" class="text-sm text-purple-600 hover:text-purple-800 underline underline-offset-2">Find books like Kingkiller →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-zinc-700 mb-2">Related reading orders</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/reading-orders/first-law" class="text-sm text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-800 transition-colors">The First Law</a>
        <a href="/reading-orders/stormlight" class="text-sm text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-800 transition-colors">Stormlight Archive</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</Layout>
